// endpoint_keep_live_workspace.proto — KeepLiveWorkspace: an agent warms one
// workspace's cache through the daemon's own keep-alive. AGENT API section.
//
// THE VERB IS THE CACHE KEEPER'S SCHEDULED BEAT, ASKED FOR NOW. The daemon
// runs the one keep-alive subroutine its scheduled beats run
// (cachelapse.Keeper.sendBeat): a parked session is restored through the
// keeper's own restore slots, the keep-alive is sent, the vendor's answer is
// awaited, and the session is stood down by the keep-alive cycle's own
// stand-down (drain.Controller.CycleDown) under that stand-down's rules. A
// session this verb started is always asked to stand down, so touching a
// parked workspace never leaves its shim up; a session that was already up
// is left to the ordinary rules, exactly as after a scheduled beat.
//
// THE VERB NEVER PAYS A COLD GATE AND NEVER INTERRUPTS WORK. A workspace at
// its cold gate is refused (its gate is passed explicitly, PassColdGate), and
// a session whose main agent is busy or whose detached work is live is
// answered `busy` with nothing sent and nothing stopped: the work keeps the
// cache warm itself.
//
